1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,388
A passenger jet lost

2
00:00:01,388 --> 00:00:03,292
its engines, one after another.

3
00:00:03,423 --> 00:00:04,403
All four.

4
00:00:04,512 --> 00:00:05,562
A strange blue glow

5
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:07,155
appeared outside the windows.

6
00:00:07,314 --> 00:00:08,202
The crew had no

7
00:00:08,202 --> 00:00:09,682
idea what was happening.

8
00:00:09,901 --> 00:00:12,234
June twenty-fourth, nineteen eighty-two.

9
00:00:12,416 --> 00:00:14,464
A Boeing flies over Indonesia.

10
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:16,161
Smoke enters the cabin.

11
00:00:16,327 --> 00:00:17,416
The aircraft can no

12
00:00:17,416 --> 00:00:18,982
longer maintain altitude.

13
00:00:19,148 --> 00:00:20,088
The pilots try to

14
00:00:20,088 --> 00:00:21,394
restart the engines.

15
00:00:21,571 --> 00:00:22,777
Again and again.

16
00:00:22,952 --> 00:00:23,998
Nothing works.

17
00:00:24,145 --> 00:00:25,587
Below them is the ocean.

18
00:00:25,807 --> 00:00:26,582
But fuel was

19
00:00:26,582 --> 00:00:27,575
not the problem.

20
00:00:27,738 --> 00:00:28,938
The aircraft had entered

21
00:00:28,938 --> 00:00:30,568
a cloud of volcanic ash.

22
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:31,907
At night, the crew

23
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:32,962
had not seen it.

24
00:00:33,092 --> 00:00:34,180
Their weather radar did

25
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:34,867
not reveal the

26
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:35,810
dry ash either.

27
00:00:35,949 --> 00:00:37,341
Inside the hot engines,

28
00:00:37,461 --> 00:00:38,536
particles melted and

29
00:00:38,536 --> 00:00:39,741
stuck to components.

30
00:00:39,891 --> 00:00:41,483
Airflow was disrupted.

31
00:00:41,617 --> 00:00:43,097
The engines flamed out.

32
00:00:43,317 --> 00:00:45,335
Then something unexpected happened.

33
00:00:45,497 --> 00:00:47,027
As the aircraft descended,

34
00:00:47,097 --> 00:00:48,402
it left the ash cloud.

35
00:00:48,557 --> 00:00:50,362
The deposits cooled, hardened,

36
00:00:50,407 --> 00:00:51,374
and broke away.

37
00:00:51,541 --> 00:00:53,029
After roughly fifteen minutes

38
00:00:53,029 --> 00:00:54,441
without thrust, the crew

39
00:00:54,441 --> 00:00:55,746
restarted the engines.

40
00:00:55,873 --> 00:00:56,810
One soon had to

41
00:00:56,810 --> 00:00:58,028
be shut down again.

42
00:00:58,249 --> 00:00:59,104
But the ordeal

43
00:00:59,104 --> 00:01:00,101
was not over.

44
00:01:00,224 --> 00:01:02,241
Ash had damaged the windscreens.

45
00:01:02,375 --> 00:01:03,587
The pilots could barely

46
00:01:03,587 --> 00:01:04,610
see the runway.

47
00:01:04,743 --> 00:01:05,801
They still managed to

48
00:01:05,801 --> 00:01:07,054
land in Jakarta.

49
00:01:07,199 --> 00:01:08,961
Everyone on board survived.

50
00:01:09,104 --> 00:01:09,742
It was not a

51
00:01:09,742 --> 00:01:10,660
massive storm that

52
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:11,951
stopped four engines.

53
00:01:12,084 --> 00:01:13,448
It was tiny particles

54
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,086
the crew had

55
00:01:14,086 --> 00:01:15,211
never even seen.
